title Season G twenty-first rung — vault seal, the password-sealed box (third composition)
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the crypto/decision-wave road; Rye-first; send each finished increment; stop at custody gates
think Read the three road docs. Season G (Cryptography) is the highest-Lindy open thread — the recent commits are a ladder of primitives (XChaCha20, HMAC, HKDF, Argon2) and the design doc names it the highest-Lindy new thread in the wave.
think Witness before narrative — ran tools/crypto_suite_witness.rish first: all twenty existing files GREEN (eighteen primitives + two compositions). The ground is solid to accrete on.
think Chose the crux: the two compositions answer custody questions — signed_carry ("who made this record"), sealed_session ("only you, by public key"). The natural third, and the stone the whole plan names Vault to stand on, is a password-sealed box ("only your password can open this"). It authors NO new cryptography — pure composition of Argon2id (GREEN) and XChaCha20-Poly1305 (GREEN), the exact pair the design doc says Vault was built toward.
think Studied the pieces: argon2.kdf(garden, out, password, salt, params, mode) needs the season arena; xchacha20.seal/open take a 24-byte extended nonce safe to draw at random. Threaded garden through seal/open. Frame binds the whole public header (magic, cost t/m/p, salt, nonce) as AEAD authenticated data, so a tampered salt or cost cannot trick open into a silent mis-derive.
think Wrote crypto/vault_seal.rye following sealed_session.rye's shape exactly — opening triad, contract asserts on every fn (>=2), named errors merged with argon2's set so KDF refusals surface honestly, copy loops not @memcpy, best-effort key wipe after use (named honestly as hygiene, not a timing claim — constant-time stays the Season horizon).
think Built GREEN on the first metal pass. tame_style_check bans clean, new file in no ratchet list.
think Wrote tools/crypto_vault_seal_witness.rish (three-cell Language/Style/Lens shape), registered it last in crypto_suite_witness.rish (dependency order — the third composition stands on all beneath), updated the suite counts (twenty-one files, three compositions) and crypto/README.md (new row, count language).
obs GREEN on the first metal pass across seven plaintext lengths (empty through 64 KiB), determinism, the fresh-salt property, and seven refusals (wrong password, tampered ciphertext/tag/salt/cost all OpenFailed with no plaintext; bad magic, bad mode, two truncations, undersized buffer, too-short and too-long salt). Whole suite re-proven GREEN across all twenty-one.
obs Purely local — TEST passwords, no real secret, no network, no funds, no real device. Sealing a real secret behind a real password stays the custody gate; the library builds and verifies, never holds a real password. No custody gate reached this round.
loom witness=crypto_vault_seal_witness green=1 plaintext_lengths=7 refusals=7 suite_files=21
